@startuml
title Strict compatibility：Dynamic Revision Round
skinparam shadowing false
actor User
participant "Host Agent / Pipeline" as Agent
participant "ResearchSpec CLI" as CLI
participant "academic-paper:revision" as Revise
participant "reviewer:re-review" as ReReview
database "Workspace" as Files

CLI --> Agent : parent-scoped round n selector
Agent -> CLI : Start tpl-pipeline-revision-round
CLI -> Files : round Start receipt + instance state
Agent -> Revise : start revision child
Revise -> Files : revision artifacts via Submit
Agent -> CLI : Advance revision-to-re-review
Agent -> ReReview : start re-review child
ReReview -> Files : verification artifacts via Submit
CLI --> Agent : accepted / revision transition candidates
Agent -> User : exact revision-outcome choices
User --> Agent : explicit workflow_branch Decision
Agent -> CLI : decide + complete round
alt accepted
  CLI -> Files : parent may advance to final-integrity
else revision
  CLI -> Files : complete round n and derive round n+1 frontier
end
note over CLI,Files
  Round identity is derived from trusted parent/child receipts.
  ARSU text does not own the counter or impose a runtime cap.
end note
@enduml
